
Comic Craft – Testing Phase

Since Comic Craft is a small project, the Testing Phase focuses on checking whether the main features work correctly and whether users can create comics without errors.

1. Purpose

The purpose of testing is to find and fix errors before the final application is delivered.

2. Main Testing Activities

1. Login Testing

Check whether:

Users can log in correctly.

Incorrect details are rejected.

Logout works properly.


2. Comic Creation Testing

Check whether users can:

Create a new comic.

Enter a comic title.

Select a layout.

Add and remove panels.


3. Editor Testing

Test the main comic editor:

Add characters.

Add backgrounds.

Add speech bubbles.

Enter text.

Move elements.

Resize elements.

Delete elements.


4. Save Testing

Check whether:

Comics can be saved.

Saved comics appear in My Comics.

Saved comics can be opened again.

Changes are stored correctly.


5. Preview/Export Testing

Check whether:

The completed comic displays correctly.

Panels appear in the correct order.

Characters and text are positioned correctly.

Export/download works if included.


3. Types of Testing

Functional Testing:
Checks whether each feature works according to the requirements.

Usability Testing:
Checks whether the interface is easy for users to understand and use.

Compatibility Testing:
Checks the application on different browsers or devices.

Performance Testing:
Checks whether the application responds reasonably quickly.

Error Testing:
Checks how the system behaves when users enter incorrect or incomplete information.

4. Sample Test Cases

Test	Expected Result

Create new comic	Comic editor opens
Add character	Character appears on the panel
Add background	Background appears correctly
Add speech bubble	Bubble appears in the panel
Save comic	Comic is saved successfully
Open saved comic	Saved content loads correctly
Preview comic	Complete comic is displayed
Delete element	Selected element is removed


5. Bug Fixing

When an error is found:

Identify Bug → Record Bug → Find Cause → Fix Bug → Test Again

For example, if a character disappears after saving, the development team identifies the problem, fixes the saving function, and tests it again.

6. Final Testing

After fixing the identified problems, the complete Comic Craft application is tested from beginning to end:

Login → Create Comic → Add Elements → Save → Open → Preview → Export

7. Expected Outcome

At the end of the Testing Phase, the major features of Comic Craft should work correctly, important errors should be fixed, and the application should be ready for the final implementation/deployment phase.
